<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-modelsdev-vercel-architecture> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Use the complete frozen models.dev provider/model catalogue as metadata and candidate authority, retain its provider npm identity for Vercel AI SDK direct adapters, resolve direct adapters through one explicit AI SDK provider registry, and keep catalogue membership, SDK support, configured route, authenticated entitlement, availability and semantic qualification as separate facts. Vercel AI Gateway is not an eligible proof route." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-subscription-host-separation> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-subscription-host-separation> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Model Codex ChatGPT and Claude claude.ai subscriptions as distinct first-party host transports, never as OpenAI or Anthropic API adapters. Bind executable/version, authenticated account mode, discovered or bounded candidate model surface, exact requested and actual identity, disabled fallback, absent API and alternate-cloud credential paths, and zero observed incremental paid cost while disclosing that the pre-existing subscription itself may be paid." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-subscription-model-closure> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-subscription-model-closure> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Join current authenticated host discovery to the frozen models.dev OpenAI and Anthropic model sets, keep aliases separate from model identities, and assign every candidate one explicit selected, eligible-unassigned, unavailable, unsupported, ambiguous or unqualified disposition. When a host exposes no exhaustive entitlement list, report the exact bounded denominator and unknowns rather than claim completeness." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-subscription-observability> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-subscription-observability> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Derive answer identity, usage, cache telemetry, cost diagnostics and useful monotonic intervals from exact bounded versioned host output bytes; missing fields remain unknown, model substitution or tool use fails closed, and live observations remain ignored route-local operational state rather than durable semantic authority." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
