<urn:usf:cost-class:subscription-zero-marginal> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "The pre-existing subscription price is outside the run incremental-cost ledger and is not claimed to be zero." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-actionable-profile> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-actionable-profile> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "The exact provider profile selects only work packets that remain actionable in this profile. One-time imported semantic-first bootstrap and foreground-lifecycle construction scopes remain evidence and governing permission/currentness resources, but are not reprojected as concurrent writers; their omission from selectsContract is neither a completion claim nor removal of the semantic-first policy or lifecycle command capability." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-census-denominator> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-census-denominator> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Partition the complete frozen models.dev provider-route and model denominator, configured V3 routes, public credential names, installed adapters, explicitly tested local agent transports and the finite reviewed legacy provider/model observation set without treating catalogue membership, a key name, historical admission or an executable as current availability or qualification." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-legacy-observations> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-legacy-observations> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Keep the names-only reviewed V2 denominator in one tracked closed file with exact permissible source content digests and explicit nonclaims. The secret-bearing untracked V2 environment source is never copied or digested; bind only the canonical names-and-reviewed-alias projection and state that disposition explicitly. The file contains the three host transports; Codex gpt-5.6-sol and gpt-5.5 observations; OpenRouter anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6; MiniMax OAuth MiniMax-M3; the direct OpenAI gpt-5.5 unavailability; the unresolved Nous openai/gpt-5.6-sol route; and the antigravity claude-opus-4.6 configured default. Every row is historical-only, excluded and UNQUALIFIED until independently configured and requalified in V3; the file contains no secret values, session identifiers, host paths or live admission authority." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-credential-containment> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-credential-containment> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Read only one explicitly selected owner-only untracked environment file; report presence only for the exact configured and reviewed mapped candidate credential-name set, retain every other public catalogue label in named denominators and aliases, and never copy, print, digest, persist or forward a credential value or reveal the selected path." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-runtime-credential-source> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-runtime-credential-source> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Treat a legacy V1/V2 environment file only as a names-only import source. Normal V3 live operations select an owner-only untracked repository-local .env or .usf/home projection containing only the exact allowlisted variables for the selected route; never copy, graph, digest or persist secret values." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-identity> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-identity> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Keep requested route, provider, route model, underlying family and model, adapter, credential name and host transport identity distinct; preserve unknown rather than guessing aliases." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-account-tier> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-account-tier> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Before provider inference, use one separately authorized provider-owned non-inference account source to admit a trusted current exact-account tier receipt proving zero paid cost, paid usage disabled, automatic overage disabled, bounded quota applicability and source authenticity; self-authored assertions, promotional credit and model prose are insufficient." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-adapter-preflight> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-adapter-preflight> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Content-verify the exact installed adapter artifact and launch it in a scrubbed child that receives only the selected credential variable, fixed origin, zero-paid ceiling, bounded tokens, timeout and no fallback before provider contact." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-authenticated-answer> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-authenticated-answer> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Acquire provider-produced answers only after current receipt and adapter gates, recording requested and actual identity, sanitized usage, quota, latency, service tier and zero-paid evidence without persisting secrets or full private transcripts." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-hidden-holdout> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-hidden-holdout> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Evaluate genuine hidden holdout cases unavailable to the answer-producing route and bind the exact provider, model, adapter, auth mode, prompt, tool, context, output, suite, corpus and policy versions; default every unmatched or missing answer to UNQUALIFIED." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-routing> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-routing> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "For every qualified work composition, make the complete current set of semantically qualified provider-model routes available for consideration; route purely from exact current census, economics, probe, authorization and task-profile facts; explain every selection, exclusion or deferral; enforce finite host and provider concurrency; and prohibit preference-based concealment plus paid or unknown fallback." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-parallelism> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-parallelism> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "At one frozen eligibility snapshot, consider every currently authorized semantically qualified provider-model route, launch every candidate admitted by useful-work and bounded provider/host concurrency policy, retain an explicit disposition for every excluded candidate, and demonstrate overlapping useful work from at least two independently qualified provider families without a Docker, GitHub, global mutation-lock or single-composer serialization bottleneck." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-token-reduction> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-token-reduction> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Compare equivalent accepted semantic workloads against a frozen baseline and report gross, useful, cached and avoided tokens, cache reuse, yield and elapsed throughput; exact scoped semantic identities key disposable repository-local cache state and cache loss changes performance only." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-test-economics> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-test-economics> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Use one table-driven pure provider matrix and one fixture-backed command chain, keep live provider calls out of the default suite, reuse scale and metrics coverage, and prune subsumed assertions rather than multiplying tests per provider or model." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-no-contact-boundary> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-no-contact-boundary> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Inventory disabled, excluded and missing-credential routes, but enforce exclusion before credential lookup, adapter construction or provider-engine construction; census and other declared no-contact operations cannot acquire run authority or contact a provider." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-policy-authorization> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-policy-authorization> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Derive one immutable effective policy as the narrowest intersection of graph, operator, task and route bounds; explicit empty allowlists deny all, unknown cost never becomes free, subscription CLI and API billing identities remain distinct, provider-owned non-inference account-source contact requires its own exact nonreplaceable authorization, and provider inference rechecks a distinct exact nonreplaceable run authorization immediately before invocation." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-model-local-currentness> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-model-local-currentness> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Keep availability, quota, cooldown, catalogue metadata, account receipt, adapter, assessment and qualification currentness model-local and durable; disappearance, restoration, expiry, metadata change or provider failure invalidates only the exact affected identity and never poisons a sibling route or fabricates healthy state." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-lazy-fair-qualification> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-lazy-fair-qualification> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Qualify only current uncovered task roles through deterministic bounded cheapest-first cohorts, count each exact model identity at most once per authorization, reconcile uncertain reservations before retry, fairly drain eligible provider queues across repeated bounded runs, and retain an explicit terminal disposition for every configured identity." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-response-identity> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-response-identity> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Bind requested and actual provider, route, model, adapter and transport identities on every response; a missing, substituted, ambiguous or unauthorized actual identity stops that route after the first response and can never fall back to a requested or default identity." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-cache-exactness> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-cache-exactness> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Key reusable prompt and result state by exact canonical provider, model, transport, semantic prefix, prompt bytes, tools, schemas, model options, context, output and policy; labels alone never alias entries, variable packet suffixes do not corrupt a stable prefix, and unknown or subthreshold provider cache behavior never authorizes a warm chain." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-useful-token-accounting> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-useful-token-accounting> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Treat missing usage, price, cache-read weight or cache-write evidence as unknown rather than zero; credit useful progress only for accepted deterministic validation, report gross and effective cost separately from target progress, and reduce utility for unnecessary tokens without rewarding unvalidated claims." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-provider-posture> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-provider-posture> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Carry an explicit provider mode, lifecycle state and readiness disposition for every route; keep health separate from authority, make unknown and revoked fail closed, and permit live-external-authorised only from current route-scoped authority and evidence. A mock, local, composed, deferred, healthy or historically configured provider never implies live readiness." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-provider-posture> <urn:usf:predicate:allowedMode> "in-memory|mock|local-test|composed-test|live-external-deferred|live-external-authorised|disabled|unavailable" <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-provider-posture> <urn:usf:predicate:allowedLifecycle> "proposed|approved-for-local-test|approved-for-composed-test|approved-for-live|suspended|deprecated|retired|revoked" <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-provider-posture> <urn:usf:predicate:allowedReadiness> "healthy|degraded|unavailable|disabled|not-configured|deferred|unauthorised|unknown" <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-port-isolation> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-port-isolation> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Make the provider boundary a typed USF port: core scheduling, routing and API surfaces depend only on the port; provider SDK imports and provider-specific response translation remain inside the content-verified adapter child; fixture fakes remain test-only and cannot satisfy live evidence." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
